Initial inspection of meta-regression_joined_data_heterogeneity_in_replication_projects.csv
(1) Structure: 86 rows x 60 columns; all schema columns present, names match exactly.
    project.x: Psychology 68, Experimental Economics 18 (project.y: rpp 68, ee 18)
    discipline: Cognitive 34, Social 34, Economics 18 (perfectly nested with project.x)
    No duplicate study IDs; 'aggregated' column entirely empty/NA.
(2) Missingness: ro, rr, fiso, fisr, discipline, project.x, relative_es, se_fiso, se_fisr: 0 missing (86/86 complete).
(3) Scale sanity: ro in [0.118, 0.86], rr in [-0.45, 0.923] (bounded [-1,1], no zeros, all ro>0).
    fiso == atanh(ro), fisr == atanh(rr) to machine precision (max dev ~4e-15) => Fisher-z confirmed.
    18 sign mismatches (ro>0, rr<0): 15 Psychology (10 Social, 5 Cognitive), 3 Experimental Economics.
    relative_es == rr/ro for 85/86 rows; exception: 'B Eitam, RR Hassin, Y Schul' (rr/ro=+0.47 but relative_es=-0.472).
    13/86 rows have relative_es > 1 (replication effect larger than original).
(4) Proposed approach (NOT yet executed):
    - Domain = discipline (primary), project.x (secondary coarser cut).
    - Paired comparison of |fisr| vs |fiso| (Fisher-z scale; abs handles sign flips).
    - Descriptives per domain: mean/median of |fisr|-|fiso| and relative_es; % pairs with |fisr|<|fiso|.
    - Paired tests: Wilcoxon signed-rank and paired t-test on |fisr|-|fiso| per domain (n=18 for Economics).
    - Sensitivity: signed (fisr-fiso); random-effects meta-analysis of z-differences using se_fiso/se_fisr;
      drop/flag Eitam anomaly row.
(5) Assumptions/uncertainties: domain definition (discipline vs project.x, nested); sign-flips treated via
    absolute magnitudes; small Economics subgroup; independence assumption for meta-analytic sensitivity.
